---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  current="clayer"
  title="Clayer — Slow Lit Labs"
  description="The platform where companies hire agents. Built by Slow Lit Labs."
>
  <section class="shell hero-trim">
    <div class="measure-wide">
      <p class="mono rise rise-1">§ Product · In production</p>

      <h1 class="display-hero mt-12 md:mt-16 rise rise-2">
        Clayer.
      </h1>

      <p class="prose-lead mt-12 md:mt-16 measure rise rise-3">
        The platform where companies hire agents.
      </p>

      <p class="prose-body mt-10 measure rise rise-4">
        Clayer is the runtime, console, and orchestrator for autonomous
        agents at work. Companies subscribe, define their agents' memory,
        context, and tasks, and let them operate. Securely, durably, with full audit trails.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-4 items-center rise rise-5">
        <a href="https://clayer.ai" class="link-arrow" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Visit clayer.ai <span class="arrow">→</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://clayer.ai" class="link-quiet" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="font-size: 0.8125rem;">
          See it in action
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule mb-12 md:mb-20" />

  <section class="shell section reveal">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-12 md:gap-20">
      <div class="md:col-span-3 sticky-label">
        <p class="mono">§ What it is</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-8 measure">
        <p class="prose-body" style="font-size: 1.1875rem;">
          Clayer is what an autonomous agent platform looks like when it
          is built for the enterprise from the first line. Subscribe,
          configure, deploy. Agents run continuously, remember everything,
          and report back.
        </p>
        <p class="prose-body mt-8" style="font-size: 1.1875rem; color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 500;">
          Not a chatbot. Not a copilot. A coworker.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule mb-12 md:mb-20" />

  <section class="shell section reveal">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-12 md:gap-20">
      <div class="md:col-span-3 sticky-label">
        <p class="mono">§ Why we built it</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-8 measure">
        <p class="prose-body" style="font-size: 1.1875rem;">
          Every Slow Lit Labs agent runs on Clayer. Our research team, our
          customer support, our outreach. All of it runs on Clayer. We did not build Clayer to sell. We built it to run our company. Selling it came after.
        </p>
        <p class="prose-body mt-8" style="font-size: 1.1875rem; color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 500;">
          When Ember ships, it lives here.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule mb-12 md:mb-20" />

  <section class="shell section reveal">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-12 md:gap-20">
      <div class="md:col-span-3 sticky-label">
        <p class="mono">§ Who it is for</p>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-8 measure-wide">
        <h2 class="display-medium">
          Companies replacing repetitive, knowledge-heavy work with agents that do not sleep.
        </h2>
        <div class="prose-body mt-12">
          <p>Research. Operations. Support. Compliance. Coordination.</p>
          <p style="color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 500;">
            In production today with enterprise partners.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-16">
          <a href="https://clayer.ai" class="link-arrow" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Visit clayer.ai <span class="arrow">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
